Derived from career-ops v1.31.0, files verify-cv-facts.mjs and
story-provenance-check.mjs:
  - the claim-shape regular expressions for counts, percentages, amounts,
    multipliers and years
  - the extraction lesson "widen the modifier window, bind lazily"

Original to fact-gate:
  - the three-way verified / unsupported / fabricated classification
  - the asymmetric comparison rules (generous verification, strict contradiction,
    qualifier-first matching)
  - lower-bound ("N+", "over N", "more than N") checking with a floor ratio, and
    approximate ("about N") checking with a tolerance
  - parenthetical-breakdown, colon-breakdown, trailing sub-count, noun-first,
    verb-qualified, participle-qualified and spelled-out count extraction
  - range extraction (both ends of "4-5 hours", "$3K–$4.5K", "40-60%")
  - the diff-as-source-of-truth parser (files, lines, test cases, dependencies)
  - measured facts ({cmd|file|json, pattern}) and their audit trail
  - structured facts input, allowlist auditing, reference-text echo downgrade,
    spelled-out tenure checking, the kind-absent rule, code-block exclusion
  - the CLI, the GitHub Action, the Claude Code hook, the JSON Schema,
    the eval harness and the tests
